  <prompt>uac-r2 pre-deploy review of tasks 203-205 on master filed issue #3034 (read it in full: gh issue view 3034). Three items:
(1) Should-fix. `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ontology/OntologyAdminRulesService.cs` `ResolvePlan` (~730) calls the static `DecisionPlanService.Resolve`, which neither logs `OntologyWriterEvents.DecisionPlanRefused` nor counts `ontology.decisionplan.refused`; only the instance `GetAsync` path does (`Services/Signals/Actions/DecisionPlanService.cs` ~99-103). The comment at ~733 claims it is counted and logged. Task 203 removed the reason code from the admin sentence, so a refused stored plan now leaves no trace.
(2) Nit. `OntologyAdminAuthoringService.cs` ~1639: one "lane" sentence ("This plan lists an action that can't be used in this rule's lane") covers PlanMalformed, UnknownAction and a non-next-step code in nextSteps, and sets no ReasonCode. Example: `{"actions":"assign-task"}` reports a lane problem.
(3) Nit. `SignalReevaluationJob.cs` ~1274: enabled policies are now sorted OrdinalIgnoreCase (task 204), not in Dataverse collation; the doc comment says the order is unchanged.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer: .NET 10 BFF, ontology admin and Signals services, OpenTelemetry metrics.</role>
  <goal>A refused stored plan on the admin Rules page is logged (event DecisionPlanRefused, with the reason) and counted (ontology.decisionplan.refused, reason tag) exactly as the decision path does; each authoring refusal gets a plain sentence that names what is actually wrong; the job's comment says what the sort does.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Reuse, don't fork: prefer a small shared helper in DecisionPlanService that both GetAsync and the admin path call to record a refusal (the static Resolve stays pure). The admin page renders often: confirm the counter is not double-counted for one page load (one row, one count) and decide whether to tag the source (e.g. surface=admin) only if the metric already has a matching tag pattern; otherwise keep the existing tags. Plain-language sentences follow task 203's style (no internal codes in what the user reads); API reason codes stay as they are; set the existing ReasonCode where the other branches set one.</background>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">No change to plan validation, refusal codes, API reason codes or the admin view shape; only logging/counting, the sentence choice and a comment.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11">No new service, interface or DI registration; a private/internal helper is enough.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene: publish-size delta vs fresh master in the PR; no new HIGH CVE; no new package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §6">Filtered BFF tests only (never the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests); full ArchTests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests fail on origin/master: the admin path logs and counts a refused plan with its reason; each of PlanMalformed, UnknownAction and the nextSteps misplacement gets its own sentence; the lane case still gets the lane sentence.</constraint>
  </constraints>
